{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Dimensionality-Reduction","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PreparedPCA","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/TSNE"],"title":"Dimensionality Reduction"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/ClusteringAndOutliers","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/VectorStoreAndRAG","doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/HNSWVectorSearch"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High-dimensional datasets frequently suffer from the “curse of dimensionality”—excessive noise, collinearity, high memory footprints, and difficulty in visualization. "},{"code":"SwiftCluster","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a suite of linear and non-linear dimensionality reduction algorithms optimized for Apple Silicon unified memory:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Exact Principal Component Analysis using singular value decomposition (SVD) with automatic CPU and UMA GPU hardware routing."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Ultra-fast approximate rank-$k$ matrix decomposition following the Halko et al. (2011) algorithm for massive datasets."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/TSNE"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Non-linear manifold learning minimizing Kullback-Leibler divergence for 2D and 3D cluster visualization."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"mermaid","code":["graph TD","    HighDim[High-Dimensional Feature Matrix X: N x D] --> Choice{Decomposition Strategy}","    Choice -->|Linear Global Variance| PCA[PCA: SVD Decomposition]","    Choice -->|Massive Dense Matrix| RSVD[RandomizedSVD: Low-Rank Projection]","    Choice -->|Non-Linear Cluster Visualization| TSNE[t-SNE: Manifold Probabilities]","    PCA --> LowDimLinear[Reduced Feature Matrix: N x k]","    RSVD --> Factors[Low-Rank Factors: U, S, Vt]","    TSNE --> Vis2D[2D\/3D Embedding Coordinates]"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"1-Principal-Component-Analysis-PCA","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"1. Principal Component Analysis (PCA)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Principal Component Analysis finds orthogonal projection axes (principal components) that maximize the variance of the data."}]},{"anchor":"Fitting-and-Transforming","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Fitting and Transforming"},{"code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ 1. Initialize PCA to extract 3 principal components","let pca = PCA(nComponents: 3, device: .auto)","","\/\/ 2. Fit and project the data matrix [N rows x D columns]","let X_reduced = try await pca.fitTransform(featureMatrix)","","\/\/ 3. Inspect explained variance ratios","if let ratios = pca.explainedVarianceRatio {","    print(\"Explained variance per component: \\(ratios)\")","    let cumulative = ratios.reduce(0.0, +)","    print(\"Total captured variance: \\(String(format: \"%.2f%%\", cumulative * 100))\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Choosing-Optimal-Components-Scree-Analysis","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Choosing Optimal Components (Scree Analysis)"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Analyze the cumulative variance to select the minimal number of components capturing $90%+$ of total data variance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var cumulativeSum = 0.0","for (index, ratio) in (pca.explainedVarianceRatio ?? []).enumerated() {","    cumulativeSum += ratio","    print(\"PC\\(index + 1): \\(String(format: \"%.3f\", ratio)) | Cumulative: \\(String(format: \"%.1f%%\", cumulativeSum * 100))\")","    if cumulativeSum >= 0.90 {","        print(\">> Recommended cutoff: \\(index + 1) components\")","        break","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"2-Approximate-Low-Rank-SVD-RandomizedSVD","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"2. Approximate Low-Rank SVD (`RandomizedSVD`)"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When factorizing large matrices where $k \\ll \\min(M, N)$, full deterministic LAPACK SVD ($O(M N \\cdot \\min(M, N))$) can be compute-intensive. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" computes an approximate rank-$k$ factorization $X \\approx U \\cdot \\text{diag}(S) \\cdot V^T$ with sketching cost $O(M N l (q + 1))$ where $l = \\min(\\min(M, N), k + p)$ (plus QR and small $l \\times N$ SVD); approximation quality depends on the matrix’s singular-value decay, oversampling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nOversamples"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and power iterations "},{"code":"nPowerIter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ Factorize a 10,000 x 500 matrix into top 20 singular components","let svdResult = try RandomizedSVD.compute(","    X: largeMatrix,","    nComponents: 20,","    nOversamples: 10,  \/\/ Oversampling p for stability","    nPowerIter: 2,     \/\/ Power iterations q for slow spectral decay","    seed: 42",")","","print(\"Left singular vectors U: [\\(svdResult.U.count) x \\(svdResult.U.first?.count ?? 0)]\")","print(\"Top singular values S: \\(svdResult.S.prefix(5))\")","print(\"Right singular vectors Vt: [\\(svdResult.Vt.count) x \\(svdResult.Vt.first?.count ?? 0)]\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-Non-Linear-Visualization-with-t-SNE","text":"3. Non-Linear Visualization with t-SNE","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While PCA preserves global variance, t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) preserves local neighborhood similarities, making it ideal for visualizing non-linear clusters, high-dimensional embeddings, and classification manifolds in 2D or 3D."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftCluster","","\/\/ 1. Initialize t-SNE actor","let tsne = TSNE(","    nComponents: 2,","    perplexity: 30.0,","    learningRate: 200.0,","    maxIterations: 1000,","    seed: 42",")","","\/\/ 2. Perform non-linear embedding","let coordinates2D = try await tsne.fitTransform(featureMatrix)","","\/\/ 3. Inspect final optimization divergence","if let klLoss = await tsne.klDivergence {","    print(\"Final KL Divergence: \\(klLoss)\")","}","","\/\/ 4. Pass coordinates to SwiftVisualization for interactive scatter plots","for point in coordinates2D.prefix(5) {","    print(\"X: \\(point[0]), Y: \\(point[1])\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"4-Hardware-Routing--Device-Selection","text":"4. Hardware Routing & Device Selection","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" accepts an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExecutionDevice"},{"type":"text","text":". See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PreparedPCA","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for numerical precision and ownership details."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Device mode"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Behavior"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".auto"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Uses the existing hardware router to choose a fitting device."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cpu"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Uses Double Accelerate LAPACK or randomized SVD, according to the selected solver."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".gpu","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Uses Float MLX conversion and centering, then SVD on the CPU stream."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".ane","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Uses the existing router fallback for unsupported ANE execution.","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"thematicBreak"}]}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/dimensionalityreduction"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftCluster"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Dimensionality Reduction & Manifold Learning"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Reduce high-dimensional feature spaces, uncover latent structures, and visualize complex datasets using PCA, Randomized SVD, and t-SNE.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/DimensionalityReduction"},"references":{"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/ClusteringAndOutliers":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/clusteringandoutliers","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/ClusteringAndOutliers","title":"Spatial Indexing, Clustering & Outlier Detection","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"High-performance clustering and density-based anomaly detection powered by ","type":"text"},{"code":"KDTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DBSCAN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"KMeans","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalOutlierFactor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"IsolationForest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/PCA":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PCA","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PCA"}],"title":"PCA","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Principal component analysis with explicit CPU solver and device choices."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Prepared inputs retain feature identity and return named, provenance-preserving scores."}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PCA","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/pca"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/TSNE":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TSNE","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TSNE","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) for non-linear dimensionality reduction and manifold learning."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/TSNE","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/tsne","title":"TSNE"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/PreparedPCA":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/PreparedPCA","title":"Fit and project prepared data with PCA","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fit preprocessing on training observations, apply the fitted preprocessing to held-out observations, and pass prepared data directly to PCA. PCA returns component scores with feature names and original row positions."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/preparedpca","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/RandomizedSVD":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/RandomizedSVD","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RandomizedSVD"}],"title":"RandomizedSVD","abstract":[{"text":"Randomized Singular Value Decomposition using the Halko et al. (2011) algorithm.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RandomizedSVD"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/randomizedsvd"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/VectorStoreAndRAG":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build low-latency semantic search, embedding retrieval, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines on Apple Silicon using SIMD Accelerate."}],"title":"In-Memory VectorStore & On-Device RAG","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/VectorStoreAndRAG","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/vectorstoreandrag"},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster/HNSWVectorSearch":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster\/hnswvectorsearch","title":"High-Dimensional Vector Search with HNSW","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster\/HNSWVectorSearch","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Scale approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) retrieval using Hierarchical Navigable Small World graphs with empirical logarithmic query scaling under navigable graph structure.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftCluster/documentation/SwiftCluster":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"PCA Dimensionality Reduction & Unsupervised Clustering."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCluster\/documentation\/SwiftCluster","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftcluster","title":"SwiftCluster"}}}